Assistant: I see the issue. The error is occurring because the TRPC queries are failing and returning undefined. Let's mock the TRPC queries and data that the component needs. We'll create a mock version of the component that doesn't rely on actual TRPC calls:

<file path="apps/web/.temp/dessn-component-routes/ConnectedVideoStep-eff0cdd4.tsx">
<change>
<description>Mock TRPC queries and data for the preview environment</description>
<content>
import React from 'react';
import { useParentState } from '../useIframeState';
import { ConnectedVideoStep } from '../../components/getting-started/steps-views/ConnectedVideoStep';
import { QueryClient, QueryClientProvider } from '@tanstack/react-query';
import { httpBatchLink } from '@trpc/client';
import { trpc } from '@calcom/trpc/react';
import { I18nextProvider } from 'react-i18next';
import i18next from 'i18next';

// Initialize i18next
i18next.init({
  lng: 'en',
  resources: {
    en: {
      translation: {
        next_step_text: 'Next Step',
      },
    },
  },
});

// Create a new QueryClient instance
const queryClient = new QueryClient({
  defaultOptions: {
    queries: {
      retry: false,
      refetchOnWindowFocus: false,
    },
  },
});

// Mock data for video apps
const mockVideoApps = {
  items: [
    {
      name: "Zoom",
      slug: "zoom",
      logo: "https://cal.com/app-store/zoom/icon.svg",
      title: "Zoom",
      description: "Video Conferencing",
      type: "zoom_video",
      userCredentialIds: [],
      dependencyData: null,
      appData: {
        location: {
          linkType: "dynamic",
        },
      },
    },
    {
      name: "Google Meet",
      slug: "google-meet",
      logo: "https://cal.com/app-store/googlemeet/icon.svg",
      title: "Google Meet",
      description: "Video Conferencing by Google",
      type: "google_video",
      userCredentialIds: [],
      dependencyData: null,
      appData: {
        location: {
          linkType: "dynamic",
        },
      },
    },
  ],
};

// Mock user data
const mockUserData = {
  metadata: {
    defaultConferencingApp: {
      appSlug: null,
    },
  },
};

// Create TRPC client with mocked responses
const trpcClient = trpc.createClient({
  links: [
    httpBatchLink({
      url: '/api/trpc',
    }),
  ],
});

// Override the actual query with mock data
queryClient.setQueryData(['viewer.integrations'], mockVideoApps);
queryClient.setQueryData(['viewer.me'], mockUserData);

export default function ComponentPreview() {
  const [state, setState] = useParentState({
    nextStep: {
      type: "boolean",
      value: false,
      label: "Trigger Next Step",
    },
  });

  const handleNextStep = () => {
    setState('nextStep', true);
    console.log('Next step triggered');
  };

  // Create a wrapper component to provide mock data
  const MockedConnectedVideoStep = (props) => {
    // Override the TRPC hooks with mock data
    trpc.viewer.integrations.useQuery = () => ({
      data: mockVideoApps,
      isPending: false,
    });

    trpc.viewer.me.useQuery = () => ({
      data: mockUserData,
    });

    return <ConnectedVideoStep {...props} />;
  };

  return (
    <trpc.Provider client={trpcClient} queryClient={queryClient}>
      <QueryClientProvider client={queryClient}>
        <I18nextProvider i18n={i18next}>
          <MockedConnectedVideoStep
            nextStep={handleNextStep}
          />
        </I18nextProvider>
      </QueryClientProvider>
    </trpc.Provider>
  );
}
</content>
</change>
</file>

I've made the following changes to fix the error:

1. Added mock data for video apps and user data that matches the expected structure
2. Created a MockedConnectedVideoStep component that overrides the TRPC hooks with mock data
3. Pre-populated the QueryClient with mock data using setQueryData
4. Overridden the TRPC query hooks to return the mock data instead of making actual API calls

The changes should resolve the "Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'map')" error by ensuring that the component always has access to the required data structure, even in the preview environment where actual API calls aren't possible.

The mock data includes:
- A list of video conferencing apps (Zoom and Google Meet as examples)
- User metadata with default conferencing app settings
- Proper typing and structure that matches what the component expects

This should now render the component properly without any undefined errors. Let me know if you see any other issues!

